.TH MCPICK 1 "2026" "mcpick" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mcpick \- choose which MCP servers a session loads, at the moment you launch it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcpick
.RI [ options ]
.B run
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B mcpick
.RI [ options ]
.BR list | doctor | measure | export | serve | import | profile
.br
.B mcpick targets
.SH DESCRIPTION
Coding agents connect to every MCP server they can find and spend context on the
tool definitions whether the session needs them or not.
.B mcpick
puts a checkbox list in front of that: it merges the servers it can see, shows
what each one costs in context, remembers what you picked, and launches the
agent with only the checked ones.
.PP
Ten agents are supported. Which mechanism is used depends on what the agent
offers: a command-line flag where one exists, an overlay of the agent's config
directory where a directory variable exists, and a rewrite-and-restore of the
project file otherwise. Run
.B mcpick targets
to see what applies to each.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR...]
Resolve a selection, render a config in the target's dialect and launch the
command. Everything after
.B run
is passed through untouched.
.TP
.B list
Print the merged catalog. With
.BR \-\-json ,
print it as JSON.
.TP
.B doctor
Connect to each selected server and report tool count, context cost, latency and
the reason for any failure. Exits non-zero if any server is unreachable.
.TP
.B measure
Connect to every server in the catalog and cache its context cost, so the picker
can show the numbers without connecting.
.TP
.B export
Print the selection in a target's dialect on standard output.
.TP
.B serve
Run mcpick itself as one MCP server fronting the selection, over stdio or, with
.BR \-\-addr ,
over HTTP. Tools are namespaced \fIserver\fB__\fItool\fR.
.TP
.B import
Seed the catalog from
.IR ~/.claude.json .
Use
.B \-\-redact
to rewrite credentials as \fB${VAR}\fR references.
.TP
.B profile \fR[\fBlist\fR | \fBsave\fR \fIname\fR | \fBdelete\fR \fIname\fR]
List the profiles in the catalog, save the selection (or \fB\-\-select\fR) as one,
or remove one.
.TP
.B login \fIserver\fR
Run the OAuth flow for a remote server: protected-resource discovery, dynamic
client registration, then an authorization-code exchange with PKCE against a
loopback redirect. The authorization URL is printed rather than opened. The
token is stored in \fI~/.mcpick/state/tokens.json\fR and attached automatically afterwards.
.TP
.B logout \fIserver\fR
Forget the stored token for a server.
.TP
.B targets
List the agents mcpick knows and how each one is reached.
.TP
.B restore
Put back every project file a session left rewritten, including sessions on
other hosts sharing the workspace. Launches do this automatically for sessions
on the same host whose process has ended.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-uid " ID"
Session id. Keys the saved selection and replaces \fB{UUID}\fR in the catalog.
Defaults to the hostname, which inside a container is the container id.
.TP
.BI \-\-file " PATH"
Catalog file. Defaults to
.I <root>/.mcp.yaml
or
.IR <root>/.mcp.json .
.TP
.BI \-\-target " NAME"
Agent dialect to render for. Defaults to the command name.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " NAME"
Use a named profile from the catalog and skip the picker.
.TP
.BI \-\-select " A,B"
Use exactly these servers and skip the picker.
.TP
.BI \-\-addr " HOST:PORT"
With
.BR serve ,
listen on HTTP instead of stdio. Only loopback addresses are accepted, because
the proxy has no authentication.
.TP
.BI \-\-home " DIR"
Where mcpick keeps everything it writes. Overrides \fB$MCPICK_HOME\fR; the
default is \fI~/.mcpick\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " DURATION"
Per-server connect timeout. Default 15s.
.TP
.B \-\-redact
With
.BR import ,
rewrite secrets as \fB${VAR}\fR references.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output for
.BR list ", " doctor " and " measure .
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-last
Skip the picker and reuse the saved selection.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Select every server and skip the picker.
.TP
.B \-\-none
Select nothing and skip the picker.
.SH KEYS
In the picker:
.BR \[u2191]\[u2193] / jk
move,
.B space
toggles (checking a server disabled in Claude Code re-enables it there at launch),
.B /
filters,
.B m
measures,
.B a
and
.B n
select all and none,
.B s
and
.B l
save and load a profile,
.B +
adds a server,
.B d
deletes one,
.B enter
launches,
.B q
aborts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <root>/.mcp.yaml
The catalog. Also read:
.IR <root>/.mcp.json .
.TP
.I ~/.mcpick/
mcpick's home, mode 0700; see \fB\-\-home\fR. It holds:
.RS
.TP
.I selections/<workspace>-<hash>/<uid>.json
The saved selection: server names only.
.TP
.I state/
OAuth tokens, measured context costs, and records for restoring project files.
.TP
.I run/
Rendered configs and overlays. They contain expanded secrets, are mode 0600, and
are removed once the process that owns them has ended.
.RE
.TP
.I ~/.claude.json
Read for project- and global-scope servers.
.TP
.I ~/.claude/plugins/
Enabled plugins' servers are read so the selection can keep them;
\fB\-\-strict\-mcp\-config\fR drops them otherwise.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MCPICK_CONFIG
Set on the launched command, pointing at the rendered config.
.TP
.B MCPICK_HOME
mcpick's home, as for \fB\-\-home\fR.
.TP
.B MCPICK_DEBUG
When set, print the exact command mcpick runs, environment and real paths
included, just before launching it.
.TP
.B MCPICK_SERVE_ALLOW_REMOTE
Set to 1 to let \fBserve \-\-addr\fR bind a non-loopback address. Only behind
authentication of your own.
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
Where Claude Code's configuration, and so \fI.claude.json\fR and plugins, live.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Located for the agents configured through it (Muse, opencode).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error, or an unreachable server under
.BR doctor .
.TP
.B 128+n
The launched command died of signal \fIn\fR.
.TP
.B 130
The picker was aborted.
.PP
Otherwise, the exit status of the launched command.
.SH EXAMPLES
Pick interactively and launch Claude Code:
.PP
.RS
.B mcpick run claude
.RE
.PP
Reuse the last selection in a script:
.PP
.RS
.B mcpick -y run codex
.RE
.PP
Find out what is eating the context window:
.PP
.RS
.B mcpick measure
.RE
.PP
Give every agent one entry that never changes:
.PP
.RS
.B mcpick --profile review serve
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
The MCP specification at
.UR https://modelcontextprotocol.io
.UE .
